y 2 of `lem:qld-sublines` gives each projected point’s marginal separately, while `eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted` assumes a joint product distribution of both line-point pairs. The stronger joint law may follow from the construction, but it is not stated or proved. The source makes the same unsupported inference at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1241-1245`; remove this redundant route or prove the joint law.\n\nF19. The PR record contains only template comments. Populate the required sections with the QPBT source ranges, the declarations introduced, known paper discrepancies, and the actual validation commands.\n\nNo Lean source or blueprint `\\lean`/`\\leanok` links changed, and the changed chapters contain no direct `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, or proof-integrity bypass. I did not rerun the build under the read-only review contract; the PR record reports successful local CI. Residual risk remains in externally imported Ji–Natarajan–Vidick–Wright–Yuen and Coladangelo–Stark results, which were checked only as represented by the in-repository source mirrors.\n\n## Verdict\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
