al.\nresults/telemetry/reviews/pr7-26b4db9fe252bc4d3fe9a71fd021b35ffee44e91.md:58:**F12.** `slugify` truncates and normalizes titles, while adoption does not compare title, body, or labels. Distinct issues can therefore reuse an old issue and even attach it to the wrong parent. Require an explicit key or reject mismatched adoption.\nresults/telemetry/reviews/pr7-26b4db9fe252bc4d3fe9a71fd021b35ffee44e91.md:60:**F13.** The current head, which commits the prior review ledger, demonstrates the feedback loop. Review artifacts should remain in runtime storage or use a defined out-of-band archival path that neither dirties the merge worktree nor changes the reviewed head.\nresults/telemetry/reviews/pr7-26b4db9fe252bc4d3fe9a71fd021b35ffee44e91.md:62:**F14-F17.** The operative documentation remains internally inconsistent: scout output is not published, several personas reference retired issue files, the new brief specifies the opposite authority model, and the amendment does not follow `local/protocols/meta.md:36-40`. These must be synchronized and covered by the hygiene tests.\nresults/telemetry/reviews/pr7-26b4db9fe252bc4d3fe9a71fd021b35ffee44e91.md:64:No Lean, blueprint, or paper-gap declarations changed, so source-statement fidelity and proof-debt checks are not applicable. `git diff --check`, shell syntax checking, and AST parsing of all extant changed Python files passed. I did not rerun the temporary-file-writing test suite in the read-only reviewer sandbox; the supplied exact-head CI status reports success. Prior round findings explicitly deferred to follow-up issues were not duplicated here.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
